          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em simplicial de Rham complex
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+manifold"} simplicial manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
            is the analog of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            may be thought of as
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
          %p
            One useful conceptual way to think of this is to notice that a a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            may be thought of as a degreewise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            and then to realize that by way of the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            such a simplicial presheaf presents an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            which we may think of as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} Lie ∞-groupoid
          .standout
            %p
              %strong> Slogan
              \. The simplicial de Rham complex is the complex of differential forms on a geometric
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
          %p We shall discuss this in more detail below.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            There are several definitions that are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet : \Delta^{op} \to Diff
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (simplicial de Rham complex, first version)
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Tot
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{A}(X_\bullet)
                    \:=
                    Tot \Omega^\bullet(X_\bullet)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
              that is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
              on the degreewise
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
              with one differential the simplicial-degree-wise de Rham differential and the other one the de Rham-degree-wise alternating sum of pullback along the face maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                                  %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi i
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi q
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi d
                                  %mi dR
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi d
                                  %mi dR
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                                  %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi i
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi q
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Omega^p(X_q) &amp;\stackrel{\sum_i (-1)^i \delta_i^*}{\to}
                    \&amp; \Omega^{p}(X_{q+1})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{d_{dR}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{d_{dR}}
                    \\\
                    \\Omega^{p+1}(X_q)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\sum_i (-1)^i \delta_i^*}{\to}
                    \&amp; \Omega^{p+1}(X_{q+1})
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            So an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \mathcal{A}(X_\bullet)
            in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is a collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ω
                    %mi q
                    %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi q
                      %mo =
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\omega^p_q \in \Omega^p(X_q))_{p+q = n}
            of ordinary differential forms.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (simplicial de Rham complex, second version)
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi Diff
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n_{Diff}
              for the standard
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              in its standard incarnations as a smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              (with boundary). These arrange in the obvious way into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi Diff
                      %mo :
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo →
                      %mi Diff
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{Diff} : \Delta \to Diff
            %p
              Say that a differential form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi q
                      %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi Diff
                      %mi p
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega^p_q \in \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^p_{Diff}\times X_q)
              is
              %em compatible
              if for each face map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_i
              we have
            %blockquote
              %p (some condition, need to look something up…)
            %p There is a decomposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi Diff
                      %mi p
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mi l
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi Diff
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi Diff
                          %mi p
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^n(\Delta^p_{Diff} \times X_q)
                    \\simeq
                    \\oplus_{k+l=n} \Omega^k(\Delta^p_{Diff})
                    \\otimes_{C^\infty(\Delta^p_{Diff} \times X_q)}
                    \\Omega^l(X_q)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This defines a bidegree and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(X_\bullet)
              is the obvious total complex of the obvious double complex here
            %blockquote
              %p will polish this up later…
          %p The following proposition says that and how these two complexes are related.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Dupont)
            %p
              Consider the map between the two
              = succeed "es" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi Diff
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^p_{Diff}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\int_\Delta : A(X_\bullet) \to \mathcal{A}(X_\bullet)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              of
              = succeed "es" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#differential_forms_on_
            Differential forms on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            A main application of this technology is to the simplicial manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G = (\cdots G \times G \stackrel{\stackrel{\to}{\to}}{\to} G \stackrel{\to}{\to} {*})
            that represents the smooth groupoid which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Dupont exhibits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+homomorphism"} Chern-Weil homomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  I(G) \to A(\mathbf{B}G)
          %p
            and constructs a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} universal G-principal-bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{E}G \to \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            (which, in traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            notation, reads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W G \to \bar W G
            – but recall that these are “Lie” simplicial groups here).
          %h2#reformulations_in_synthetic_differential_geometry Reformulations in synthetic differential geometry
          .query
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              \: This section is supposed to provide a useful reformulation of the simplicial de Rham complex in the context described at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+theory"} ∞-Lie theory
            %p In the language uses there, the statement we establish is the following:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_{th}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi sPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                      %mi loc
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} = (sPSh(C)_{proj}^{loc})^\circ
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              of
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} Lie ∞-groupoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+contractible+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} locally contractible (∞,1)-topos
              (as discussed there). Accordinly we have its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} path ∞-groupoid
              and
              %span.newWikiWord
                infinitesimal path ∞-groupoid
                %a{:href => "/schreiber/new/infinitesimal+path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ?
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Π
                        %mi inf
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(-)
            %p Then
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Π
                          %mi inf
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X)
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
                  to the simplicial de Rham complex
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi Π
                          %mi inf
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        CE( \Pi^{inf}(X)) \simeq \mathcal{A}(X_\bullet)
                        \\,.
          %p The following discussion breaks this down and then describes the proof.
          %p
            As a preparation, recall from the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+in+synthetic+differential+geometry"} differential forms in synthetic differential geometry
            that if we pass from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{T},R)
            that models the axioms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{T}
            there is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+singular+simplicial+complex"} infinitesimal singular simplicial complex
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi inf
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})} : \Delta^{op} \to \mathcal{T}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            that in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplices
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            As discussed there, this is such that under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+algebra"} cosimplicial algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom( X^{\Delta^\bullet_{inf}}, R )
            maps to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            (and under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            to the full
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+dg-algebra"} de Rham dg-algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi Moore
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_{Moore} :
                  C^\infty( X^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf}}))
                  \\mapsto
                  \\Omega^\bullet(X)
                  \\,.
          %p It would be nice to have an analog of this statement for simplicial objects and the simplicial de Rham complex. I am thinking that the answer should be the following:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet : \Delta^{op} \to \mathcal{T}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            that is degreewise of the sort such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+singular+simplicial+complex"} infinitesimal singular simplicial complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_n)^{\Delta^\bullet_{inf}}
            exists. Use that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            is canonically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} tensored
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            to find that simplicial objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            are canonically tensored over
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %em realization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Π
                    %mi inf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Δ
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msubsup
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi inf
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X_\bullet) := \int^{[n] \in \Delta}
                  \\Delta[n] \cdot X_n^{(\Delta^{\bullet}_{inf})}
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
                is the standard
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            %li
              %p the integrand is the tensor operatoin of simplicial objects by simplicial sets
            %li
              %p
                the integral sign denotes the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
          %p
            By the lemma
            %em expression in terms of simplicial realization
            at
            %span.newWikiWord
              infinitesimal path ∞-groupoid
              %a{:href => "/schreiber/new/infinitesimal+path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ?
            this is the same as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Π
                      %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X)
          %p The above proposition now reads in pedestrian terms:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore cochain complex
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+algebra"} cosimplicial algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Π
                      %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Π
                      %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X_\bullet)) := Hom_{\mathcal{T}}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X_\bullet),R)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
              to the simplicial de Rham complex of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We use the cosimplicial and the simplicial version of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+theorem"} Eilenberg-Zilber theorem
              together with the fact that for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+set"} bisimplicial set
              the diagonal is given by the realization (as discussed there)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Diag
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Δ
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diag F_{\bullet,\bullet} \simeq \int^{[n] \in \Delta} \Delta[n] \cdot F_{n,\bullet}
              to compute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Π
                              %mi inf
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo :
                            %mo =
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi n
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msubsup
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi inf
                                  %mo •
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Diag
                            %msubsup
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi inf
                                  %mo •
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi C
                            %mi Diag
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi inf
                                  %mo •
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ≃
                              %mrow
                                %mi q
                                %mi i
                            %mi Tot
                            %mi C
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi inf
                                  %mo •
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Tot
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    C ( C^\infty(\mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X_\bullet)) )
                    \&amp; :=
                    C ( Hom( \int^{[n]} \Delta[n] \cdot X_n^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})}
                    , R))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    C ( Hom( Diag X_\bullet^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})} , R))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    C Diag Hom( X_\bullet^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})} ,R)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq_{q i}
                    Tot C Hom( X_\bullet^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})} ,R)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Tot \Omega^\bullet(X_\bullet)
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Here in the last step we used the following reasoning on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+object"} bisimplicial object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi p
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi inf
                            %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([p],[q]) \mapsto (X_p)^{(\Delta^q_{inf})}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for fixed
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+algebra"} cosimplicial algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi p
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi inf
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom((X_p)^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})},R)
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_p
                  – this is the statement about combinatorial
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+in+synthetic+differential+geometry"} differential forms in synthetic differential geometry
              %li
                %p
                  for fixed
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+algebra"} cosimplicial algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi inf
                              %mi q
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom((X_\bullet)^{((\Delta^q_{inf}))}, R)
                  is the complex of functions on simplices whose differential is the alternating sum of pullbacks along face maps – by the very definition of the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
            %p This means that the simplicial de Rham complex is (quasi-isomorphic to) the total complex of the bi-cosimplicial algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Tot
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi inf
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{A}(X_\bullet) \simeq
                    Tot C(Hom((X_\bullet)^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})}, R))
                    \\,.
            %p
              So it remains to show that this total complex is also (quasi-isomorphic to) the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Π
                        %mi inf
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X_\bullet),R)
              %a{:href => "http://www.maths.abdn.ac.uk/~bensondj/papers/g/goerss-jardine/ch-4.dvi"} exercise 1.6 here
              which says (transported from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              to
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              of our
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+object"} bisimplicial object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi inf
                          %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi inf
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d((X_\bullet)^{\Delta^\bullet_{inf}})
                    \\simeq
                    \\int^{[n]} \Delta^n \cdot (X_n)^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This implies that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Π
                      %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X_\bullet),R)
              is the Moore complex of the diagonal of the bisimplicial algebra
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi inf
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X_\bullet^{(\Delta^\bullet_{inf})}),R)
            %p This way the desired statement recudes to the quasi-isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi diag
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Π
                      %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Tot
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Π
                      %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    diag (Hom(\mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X_\bullet),R)
                    \\simeq
                    Tot (Hom(\mathbf{\Pi}_{inf}(X_\bullet),R)
                    \\,.
            %p
              But this (even their chain-homotopy equivalence) is the content of the generalized
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+theorem"} Eilenberg-Zilber theorem
          %h2#references References
          %p
