                %em Curvature and Characteristic Classes
          %blockquote
            %p (I am still looking for the best survey reference…)
          %p
            When restricted to low degree this is closely related to or synonymous to considerations of de Rham cohomology in the context of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
          %blockquote
            %p (need to dig out references)
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
            for simplicial manifolds was proven in the classical
          %ul
            %li#BottShulmanStasheff76
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"}> Raoul Bott
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herbert+Shulman"} Herbert Shulman
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the de Rham theory of certain classifying spaces
              = succeed "," do
